body:
## Problem

If you have a manifest with a resolution + override, currently we drop the override, as this information is not easily available on the lock. This means that the commands will be executed in a different way, this is especially important when dealing with 32bits OCaml

## Solution

This is a workaround, but if the source is `github:` and there is a single override on the lock, we copy it to the resolution

## Example
If you run generate on this manifest below the problem shows, as it will add just the source
```ocaml
{
  "dependencies": {
    "ocaml": "*"
  },
  "resolutions": {
    "ocaml": {
      "source": "esy-ocaml/ocaml#dd66cad318e04c7f2c753f8ce2fd8851e975f89a",
      "override": {
        "build": [
          [
            "./esy-configure",
            "--prefix",
            "$cur__install",
            "--build=x86_64-pc-linux-gnu",
            "--host=i386-linux",
            "CC=gcc -m32",
            "AS=as --32",
            "ASPP=gcc -m32 -c",
            "PARTIALLD=ld -r -melf_i386"
          ],
          "./esy-build"
        ]
      }
    }
  }
}
```
